ENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19a2a4ff85&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","login":"KoBeWi","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99911#pullrequestreview-2572576212","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99911","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-01-24T12:52:20Z"},{"id":2613394129,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6bxTrR","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- **Bake CollisionShape2D** should be renamed to **Bake CollisionShape2D(s)**, as it can create multiple collision shapes in a single operation if the collision shape is convex but the combiner's shape is concave. When the collision shape is concave, it will also occur if the CSG combiner has multiple disjoint shapes in it. This does not occur with other baking types (even Polygon2D, surprisingly).\r\n- **Bake Polygon2D** does not reuse the vertex color that was defined in CSGCombiner2D, so it resets to white. In comparison, the color is preserved when baking to MeshInstance2D.","html_url":"http