est_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99911","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-19T21:42:32Z"},{"id":3301897345,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7EzvSB","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"As mentioned above there are some orthogonal use cases and solutions in this context. Personally I think 2D CSG is great for prototyping and constructing more complex shapes and then baking them. Being node-based this empowers code-challenged users to conveniently create and modify interesting shapes with collisions enabled. I think eventually more multi-shape operations should be added to Geometry2D or some other low-level interface exposed to scripting (wrapping Clipper2) and 2D CSG should be calling them (instead of using Clipper2 directly), but that can be done later.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99911#pullrequestreview-3301897345","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99911","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-10-04T14:19:43Z"}]